To achieve this, we will utilize our experience with API gateways such as Kong and Apigee, which will enable us to create interfaces of API type as required by con32. We will also employ our knowledge of message brokers like Apache Kafka and RabbitMQ to facilitate communication between the various systems.

For high availability, we will deploy the solution on a cloud infrastructure that provides redundancy and failover capabilities. Given our experience with cloud providers such as OVHcloud, Scaleway, and Outscale (SecNumCloud), we can ensure that the solution is deployed in a secure and reliable environment. Our expertise in containerization using Docker and Kubernetes (K8s) will also enable us to design a highly available and scalable architecture.

To guarantee an availability of 99.9%, we will implement monitoring tools such as Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK stack to ensure that the solution is running smoothly and that any issues are quickly identified and addressed. Our experience with infrastructure as code (IaC) tools like Terraform and Ansible will enable us to automate the deployment and management of the infrastructure, further ensuring high availability.

In terms of specific technical components, we propose using a combination of our AI/ML stack, including LLM models such as Mistral 7B or LLaMA 3, and RAG frameworks like LangChain or LlamaIndex. We will also utilize vector databases like Qdrant or Weaviate to store and manage the data. For inference servers, we can use vLLM or Ollama, which will enable us to provide fast and accurate responses to the agents' queries.

Overall, our proposed architecture is designed to meet the client's technical constraints while providing a highly available, scalable, and secure solution that leverages our expertise in API integration, cloud architecture, and data engineering.
